---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const seo = {
  page_description: "Privacy Policy for The Cayman Journal.",
  canonical_url: "/legal/privacy/",
  no_index: true
};
---
<Layout seo={seo} title="Privacy Policy | The Cayman Journal">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-16 px-6 prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: October 2023</p>
    <p>The Cayman Journal ("we", "our", or "us") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you visit our website.</p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect personal data that you voluntarily provide to us when you subscribe to our newsletter, fill out a contact form, or use our interactive tools (e.g., saving tool results to your email). This includes your email address, name, and any specific data points you submit into our forms.</p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information we collect to send you our newsletter, respond to your inquiries, and provide you with requested tool results. We do not sell your personal data to third parties.</p>

    <h2>3. Data Storage</h2>
    <p>Form submissions are securely stored using our capture API provider. We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your data.</p>

    <h2>4. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us via our Contact Page.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
